(project tuna-accounts
 (doc "Tuna book chapter: the pp-slice - tuna as a pricklypear-like live habitat slice. Two credential tiers over ONE identity store (bearer tokens for agents, opaque cookie sessions for browsers), admin-only identity minting with non-admin defaults, and the anonymous public rim (welcome, /code, /agent.txt, /.well-known/agent.json, /src.tgz). Research question, stated so it can be refuted: a tree-calculus habitat whose access law is already 'the route record is the capability' (borg/routes.borg law 3) needs NO second permission matrix for a human tier - browser sessions can ride the same identities rows and the same path-prefix grants, so the whole pp-slice lands as additive credential tables plus reserved public surfaces, never a new authz model.")
 (status implemented)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section accounts
  (doc "The identity store stays singular: `identities` (0001) is the one subject table; the pp-slice adds credentials, sessions, and an audit log beside it, and the public face is reserved surfaces that match before the route dispatcher (routes.borg law 2). Nothing here resolves names at a prim boundary - grants remain arguments (AGENTS 7).")
  (status implemented)
  (subsection credential-tiers
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
      Tuna has ONE subject table (`identities`, migration 0001;
      `is_admin` gates only the four admin acts - mint identities,
      route publish, grant admin view, others' grants) and now two
      credential tiers over it, both resolving to a `Store.identity`:

      BEARER (agent tier, unchanged).  `Authorization: Bearer
      <token>` on every `/api/*` route; sha256 stored in
      `identities.token_hash`; boot mints root (TUNA_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN,
      printed once) and fed peers per TUNA_FED_PEERS.

      SESSION (human tier, the pp-slice).  Migration 0013 adds
      `credentials(kind, secret_hash, unique(identity_id, kind))`,
      `auth_sessions(token_hash, expires_at, revoked_at)` and
      `auth_log`.  POST /login accepts username+password OR a bearer
      token; BOTH mint an opaque session row (32 random bytes hex;
      only its sha256 is stored; 14-day TTL) and set the
      `tuna_session` cookie HttpOnly + SameSite=Lax.  The cookie
      carries ONLY the session token - it supersedes the v0 stance
      where the cookie carried a raw bearer.  Logout revokes the
      row.  `Api.authenticate` keeps bearer FIRST (agents) and falls
      back to the session cookie (browser clients on /api/*).

      INTERIM HASHING, NAMED.  `credentials.secret_hash` uses the
      PP-compatible interim string `sha256$salt$digest` with
      `digest = sha256(salt_hex ^ ":" ^ password)`, salt from
      /dev/urandom.  Not a memory-hard KDF; argon2id is the planned
      drop-in and the format is string-compatible so a future
      upgrade verifies legacy rows and transparently rehashes on
      success - no flag day.  Verify is constant-time; an unknown
      username is timing-flattened against a fixed dummy hash so the
      endpoint does not oracle account existence.  No CSRF token and
      no login throttle yet; `auth_log` exists so a throttle/forensics
      pass has data instead of guesses.

      BOOT.  `TUNA_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD` (optional) ensures root's
      password credential each boot; setting a new value rotates it.
      Unset means no insecure default - root signs in by its bearer
      OIDC (chatgpt sign-in, 0018, DORMANT).  The browser tier's
      agentless path: `GET /login/chatgpt` stores a one-shot state row
      (`oidc_logins`: only sha256(state) stored, with the PKCE verifier
      + nonce it guards, 10-minute expiry), then 303s to OpenAI's
      authorize endpoint (code + PKCE S256).  The callback consumes the
      state atomically, exchanges the code at the token endpoint over
      TLS (client_secret_post), validates the id_token claims
      (iss/aud/exp/iat/nonce - signature NOT verified in v1, named
      follow-up like the interim password hashing), cross-checks the
      userinfo sub, and provisions the identity over the SAME signup
      path (name law + garden grant, one transaction; filler bearer
      token never revealed).  14-day session mint; `auth_log` kind
      'chatgpt'.  Dormant unless TUNA_CHATGPT_CLIENT_ID+SECRET are set:
      routes answer 404, login page shows no button.
      TUNA_CHATGPT_ISSUER overrides the issuer (default
      https://auth.openai.com); TUNA_CHATGPT_REDIRECT_URI overrides the
      derived redirect (<origin>/login/chatgpt/callback).

      token at the login page's token form. |))))
  (subsection identity-minting
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
      Identity minting is the ONE admin gate that is not a grant
      (the subject exists before any grant can reference it):
      `POST /api/identities` and the `/identities` htmx page mint a
      NON-ADMIN identity by default (`admin=true` is an explicit
      opt-in) and return its bearer token ONCE alongside an optional
      initial password.  `GET /api/identities` is the roster, no
      token hashes.  A non-admin gets 403 on mint.

      BOUNDARY AUDIT (the plan's T2 question).  A non-admin identity
      already behaves as intended because the authority is the grant
      row, not the identity kind: it can run/compile, keep its own
      REPL dictionary (per-identity dest), mint/attenuate/revoke its
      OWN grants (store holder checks), and read public pages.  It
      cannot mint identities (new is_admin gate), revoke others'
      grants (holder check), or write outside its path-prefix garden
      (grants are the only capability at a prim boundary, and route
      publish requires a covering grant).  No second permission
      matrix was added - the audit found no hole that needed one. |))))
(* agent note (|2026-10-16 g1 ENFORCEMENT (owner decision 2026-10-15,
        board card todo/g1-allowlist-deny-all): the boundary audit above
        held at the prim boundary from the start, but the DIRECT host API
        (/api/tree/get, /api/tree/put incl. CAS, /api/tree/list) was the
        gap - any authenticated identity could read/write/list any path
        under the old "the host API is the operator surface" stance
        (retired).  Agent tree ops are now deny-all with explicit grants:
        every op requires a live covering grant of the caller
        (path_prefix covers the op path, NULL prefix covers everything),
        admins bypass - the same rule as route publish/delete
        (api.ml tree_allowed/deny_tree).  Denials are journaled op rows.
        verify-1 [1.6] pins the floor: grantless 403s journaled, a
          covering grant opens exactly its prefix, admin bypass.  OPEN
          TOOTH CLOSED 2026-10-26 (mint-time scoping): the public mint
          ignored path_prefix (noted in board_probe), so a member's
          scoped-looking mint was really a store-wide one and only the
          mint-then-attenuate dance reached a prefix.  POST /api/grants
          now stores a validated path_prefix (an explicit "" is REFUSED -
          prefix_match "" covers everything) and checks prim against the
          registry ("*" is the wildcard); /grants/mint shares the same
          rules.  verify-1 [1.6] keeps pinning the floor through the
          attenuate route.  TOOTH CLOSED 2026-10-27 (the tenancy law; the
          note at the end of this file): a NULL prefix now covers NO path,
          so a store-wide row is a pathless capability, not a master key.
          What remains is the refinement the tenancy note records - the
          floor is still path-only and prim-blind, so a garden is a prefix
          rather than a per-prim allowlist.|) *)

(* agent note (|2026-10-16 g2 RUNNER TOKENS (the glochid issue-token
        precedent, PP run-primitive.borg §identity + POLICY-5; board card
        todo/g2-parity-identities): tuna identities are now at Bearer
        PARITY with the bridge law - an operator (admin) issues a NAMED,
        individually revocable Bearer to an identity for a runner to hold
        (migration 0016 runner_tokens; api.ml /api/identities/:id/tokens
        mint|list|revoke), the raw token leaves the process exactly once,
        and a live token authenticates as the SAME identity row at FULL
        bearer parity (authenticate falls back to verify_runner_token),
        so grants and the g1 tree-op floor apply unchanged.  Revocation
        is the whole lifecycle (no TTL); the identity's primary token is
        never shared with the runner and survives a revoke.  ONE IDENTITY
        PER RUNNER stays the PP law: mint the identity, then issue its
        runner token.  verify-1 [1.7] pins: issue -> parity use -> floor
        403 -> covered put 201 -> revoke -> 401, primary intact.  D4 Q5
        (per-runner identities with deny-all allowlists) is now drivable
        end to end against tuna.|) *)

(* agent note (|2026-10-16 a1 RUN VISIBILITY (board card
        todo/a1-run-authz): run rows are attributable to their caller,
        and the run-scoped API now enforces it - get/journal/deriv/
        trace/fork/live-replay/gc answer to the owning identity and
        admins (404 to anyone else, no existence leak), list_runs
        scopes non-admins to their own runs, and the verify sweep is an
        operator surface (all=1 is admin-only; the status view is
        caller-scoped).  Rows with no caller (pre-attribution v0 rows)
        answer to admins only.  The public /code browser stays a server
        page, not this law.  Wrinkle recorded: fork_journal inherits
        the parent's caller, so an admin fork of a member's run is
        attributed to the member - defensible for counterfactual
        history, revisit if forks become a user-facing act.|) *)

(* agent note (|2026-10-16 a5 COOKIE HARDENING (board card
        todo/a5-cookie-csrf): the Dream-style ~encrypt/~decrypt flags
        were ceremony - the cookie carries only an opaque server-side
        session token - and are gone; name/value/path are sanitized
        (separators or control characters would craft arbitrary
        Set-Cookie attributes); the clearing cookie now matches the
        session cookie's HttpOnly; Secure rides TUNA_COOKIE_SECURE
        (unset = loopback dev, the deploy env file sets it behind the
        TLS edge).  The CSRF limitation is enumerated honestly in the
        README (the mutating GET is get_run's auto replay-verify; the
        all=1 sweep is admin-only since a1) - a real CSRF token stays
        the named future fix.|) *)
  (subsection public-rim
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
      The hard-public face is reserved (routes.borg law 2 list grew
      by this book change: welcome, code, agent.txt, src.tgz,
      .well-known, identities), so a route record can never shadow
      it.  All anonymous, matching before the route dispatcher:

      /welcome   front page: what tuna is, the calculus in two
                 lines, links to /code, the manifests, /src.tgz,
                 /login, /health.
      /code      read-only browser for newest programs + runs
                 (data-first; a server page, not a route record,
                 because it carries no capability and lists dynamic
                 rows - recorded call per the routes chapter).
      /agent.txt / /.well-known/agent.json   agent manifest
                 generated in OCaml (server/lib/agent.ml, shaped
                 after PP's agent_discovery): auth model, first
                 calls, endpoint census, replay + deriv verify
                 surfaces, htmx hints.  Base URL derived from the
                 request's forwarded host headers, so it is correct
                 behind a reverse proxy.
      /src.tgz   the server's own source at HEAD.  Generated by
                 scripts/deploy/build-public.sh (`git archive HEAD`,
                 no _build, no secrets) into TUNA_PUBLIC_DIR and
                 served from disk by Dream.from_filesystem - no
                 github dependency at serve time.  Reflects HEAD at
                 the last build-public run, not necessarily the
                 running binary.
      /health    tokenless liveness, unchanged. |))))
  (subsection acceptance
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
      1. PUBLIC SURFACES.  Against a live isolated instance,
         /welcome /code /agent.txt /.well-known/agent.json /health
         answer 200 anonymously; /src.tgz is a valid gzipped tar;
         unknown public paths are plain 404.  `scripts/smoke-public.sh`.
      2. SESSION TIER.  Password login mints a session cookie; the
         cookie drives /api/*; logout revokes it and the same cookie
         then 401s.  Bearer still works on /api/*; unauthenticated
         /api/* is 401.  `tests/session_tests.ml` (PG-gated, own
         scratch db) + smoke-public [10].
      3. MINTING.  An admin mints a NON-ADMIN identity + password;
         the returned bearer token authenticates; the minted identity
         is 403 on identity mint; the admin /identities page shows
         the form and a non-admin sees an explanation, not the form.
         smoke-public [8][9][11].
      4. BOOK/REALITY.  `borge lint && borge report` clean; the
         routes reserved list transcribed in server/lib/routes.ml
         matches the pinned list in borg/routes.borg.

      OUTCOMES 2026-10-02 - green.
      - T1 (0013) + tests/session_tests.ml green under scratch db.
      - T2 API + /identities page; smoke-public [8][9] green.
      - T3 public face (agent.ml + pages/public.ml + src.tgz slot);
        smoke-public [1]-[6][12] green.
      - T4 scripts/serve.sh + scripts/deploy/{build-public.sh,
        tuna.service,reverse-proxy.md}; serve.sh start boots PG +
        migrations + build + src.tgz + server on :18092.
      - T5 this chapter + only one inline line in tuna.borg; full
        `dune build @all && dune runtest tests` green, all three
        smokes (public + api + ui) green against :18092. |))))
  (subsection pre-registered-failures
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
      F10 SESSION CONFUSION.  The two credential tiers drift into
      two authorization models (a session that is implicitly more
      privileged than its bearer, or a second permission matrix
      beside the grant rows).  TRIGGER: any pp-slice change that
      resolves a session to anything other than its identity's
      grants + is_admin.  THEN: it is a book issue - the authority
      is the grant row (AGENTS 7); revert, or amend this chapter
      and routes.borg together in the open.

      F11 RIM SHADOWING.  A route record begins serving a reserved
      public path (a stale reserved list, a new /src-like surface
      added in code without the book change).  TRIGGER: dispatch
      answers a reserved site path, or the transcribed list in
      routes.ml diverges from borg/routes.borg.  THEN: the book
      change lands FIRST (the list grows by book change, never in
      code), the code list follows in the same commit, and a
      regression test pins the collision denial. |)))))
)

(* agent note (|2026-10-27 TENANCY (the floor law the g1 note left open;
     live-box scoping pass 2026-10-27): a grant's path_prefix must COVER
     the path a call touches, and a NULL prefix covers NO path.  Three
     consumers, one law: has_covering_grant (store.ml) ignores NULL rows,
     so a holder's capability is the union of its SCOPED rows - one
     store-wide row no longer stands in for every garden; check_grant's
     NULL arm answers Prefix_denied for any call that carries paths, so a
     pathless capability authorizes only pathless calls at the prim
     boundary too; attenuation_narrower refuses to derive path scope from
     a NULL parent, so scope can only ever narrow.  The mint completes it
     (Api.grant_mint_core): a non-admin mint of a path-addressed prim
     (tree/*, ns/fork, "*") needs an explicit prefix INSIDE a prefix the
     caller already covers, and an admin may mint FOR another identity
     ({"identity": "<id>"}) - the operator seeds a garden, the member
     narrows inside it, and neither can mint into somebody else's space
     or hand a capability to somebody else.  /api/tree/log and
     /api/tree/state now answer to the floor with the requested prefix as
     the path (both took _auth and folded the whole substrate for any
     bearer).  verify-1 [1.6]/[1.7] and verify-14 [14.1] pin: NULL rows
     deny, a seeded garden opens exactly its prefix, a member cannot mint
     outside its own or for another identity, "" is 400.  STILL OPEN: the
     floor stays path-only and prim-blind, so a garden is a prefix and not
     a per-prim allowlist (no read-without-write row shape); raw-string
     prefix matching aliases siblings (u.notes covers u.notes-writer),
     and separator-aware matching must keep the garden-root listing
     working, since tree/list gates on the request's prefix string
     itself.|) *)

(* agent note (|2026-10-27 GRANTS PAGE READ-ONLY: the human /grants page
      is a read view of the grants table (short id, identity, prim,
      path_prefix, status, granted_by, created_at) over the same
      Store.list_grants the admin JSON list uses; the session-tier form
      endpoints /grants/mint + /grants/:id/revoke are retired.  Minting
      and revocation stay API-first - POST /api/grants,
      /api/grants/:id/attenuate and /api/grants/:id/revoke are the
      machine surface, and the page's muted note says so.  smoke-ui
      [15] pins the read-only page (table renders, no forms ship). |) *)
